By Sarah DiGregorio

YIELD:8 servings
TIME:1 hour and 5 minutes

This dish has all of the crispy-melty-tomatoey appeal of a chicken or eggplant Parmesan, but it uses only one pot. Olive oil provides richness, and broiling lends a cheesy crunch without the mess of breading and frying. The pizzalike flavors and mellow cauliflower make it a (potentially) kid-friendly meal. Feel free to omit the olives if that makes more sense for your family. In fact, this dish is hig…";}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:3:"mcf";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1638472459;s:8:"modified";i:1638472479;}s:7:"creator";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:11:"last_change";a:8:{s:4:"date";i:1638472479;s:2:"ip";s:13:"71.210.40.185";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:37:"recipes:roasted_cauliflower_and_farro";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:-1;}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:3:"mcf";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";}}}